title: Grace, Not Works – Saved by Grace Through Faith
description: Salvation is the free gift of God by grace through faith in Christ, never earned, kept or paid for by our works: the teachings on grace, not works, in the King James Bible.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-salvation-grace-not-works.html

# Built from the author's teachings on the theme "Grace, not works" in studies/data/topics/salvation.json.
# Every paragraph is the author's own wording, trimmed; the slide titles are plain labels.

=== Introduction
# from 12911, 6040
--- Grace, Not Works [title]
overline: Doctrine · Salvation
heading: Grace, Not Works
sub: Salvation by grace through faith without works has been the Gospel from the beginning.
refs: Ephesians 2:8-9; Romans 4:5; Titus 3:5
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 4604, 6040
--- By grace are ye saved
big: Ephesians 2:8-9 | mark: Not of works, lest any man should boast
lead: Grace is unmerited, unearned and unconditional love.
p: That works are not how we are saved is the clearest, most repeated doctrine in scripture, and yet it continues to be the stumbling block that keeps so many perishing, damned to Hell because they trust in their self righteousness to save them.

=== What grace is
# from 8964
--- Grace cannot be earned
lead: Grace is the unearned, unmerited, undeserved gift given by God from His mercy and love.
p: It’s not a spiritual, magical “force” like Star Wars. It doesn’t come in portions. You don’t need reups and you cannot earn it. It is the favor of God to redeem you in Christ, despite you deserving death and Hell. It is an expression of His love towards us.
big: Romans 11:6 | mark: if by grace, then is it no more of works

# from 10778, 10780, 1959
--- Grace, not debt
scripture: Romans 4:4-5 | mark: to him that worketh not
p: If it were of works, that means God would be indebted to us. To pay us for our works. That we were owed. **Debt is deserved. Grace is undeserved.**
panel-warn: “I must work to be saved, or to stay saved” | When someone says their salvation or their ability to stay saved is contingent on their works, they are saying they are good enough to please God. That they are owed salvation. That the glory is theirs.
panel: Grace is not transactional | Love is not transactional. Grace is not contingent on conditions, because it is unearned. Undeserved. Unconditional love.

=== No flesh justified by works
# from 10750
--- Every mouth stopped
scripture: Romans 3:19-20 | mark: by the deeds of the law there shall no flesh be justified in his sight
p: That is the purpose of the law, to serve to humble us and reveal the holiness of God, that we may come to call upon His name to be saved.
callout: It is impossible for man to work their way to Heaven. We cannot attain the righteousness of God.

# from 12434, 5309
--- The ledger of sin
kicker: Numbers 5
lead: The concept of the ledger and the debt incurred by sin is given that we may know we can never do enough to offset it. Our only hope is in Christ.
p: God demands payment plus the fifth, which when you consider the sins of man in a given day, if all were to be covered, even a righteous and godly man could be bankrupt by the end of a few days. [[Numbers 5:6-7]]
p: If you believe that you have to work for your salvation, that Jesus needs your help to impute his righteousness over your filthy rags, then what must you do to be saved? The Bible makes it clear: Keep the whole of the law. But if you offended one point, Hell awaits you. [[James 2:10]]

# from 10750
--- Justified freely by his grace
scripture: Romans 3:23-26 | mark: Being justified freely by his grace
p: We are justified freely by His grace. Even the righteousness of God, **that is by faith**, upon **all them that believe**.
p: That’s the good news. This is the Gospel.

# from 10750
--- Therefore we conclude
big: Romans 3:28
p: Read that again. Say it out loud. Three chapters of building argument against the judaizers, the works-based false gospel.
p: There is no one who reads this and says “yeah, but you have to do works” who is seeking truth. [[Romans 3:27]]

=== Pictures from the beginning
# from 6500, 6543
--- Fig leaves and Cain’s offering
panel-warn: Fig leaves | The first instinct Adam and Eve had, when faced with this feeling of shame, was to attempt to cover it up with their own works. And like our own works, the fig leaves were insufficient to make them righteous. [[Genesis 3:7]]
panel-warn: Cain’s fruit of the ground | Cain brought his works and was rejected. [[Genesis 4:3-5]]
panel: Abel’s lamb | The firstling lamb. The sacrifice of blood for atonement. The Bible says Abel *by faith* brought the sacrifice that was acceptable unto the Lord. [[Hebrews 11:4]]
callout: How many of us seeking our own righteousness, poorly sow together fig leaves of our own works, seeking to erase the transgressions ourselves. Hiding from God?

# from 10782, 10778
--- Abraham, before circumcision
fig: Counted unto him for righteousness | Genesis 15:6; Romans 4:3
scripture: Romans 4:10-11 | mark: Not in circumcision, but in uncircumcision
p: Abraham did not receive the ordinance of circumcision until decades after his believing God’s promise, and being saved by that faith.
p: There is no rite or ordinance that is required for salvation. Not baptism. Not any ritual or keeping of tradition. No works of the law.

# from 11429, 12503
--- Saved by the blood before the law
lead: Salvation is front loaded and found only by faith. For the salvation of Israel from bondage and death came by faith alone, by the blood.
tile: 1 | **The Passover blood.** The salvation out of sin of Egypt had already taken place. [[Exodus 12:13]]
tile: 2 | **The sea.** The baptism of the waters of the sea followed. [[1 Corinthians 10:1-2]]
tile: 3 | **The law.** The understanding of the law given.
tile: 4 | **Sanctified.** Then they were told to sanctify themselves, for their own good and to better serve God’s will.
panel-warn: Turn from sin first | Those telling others they must turn from their sins first before they can believe are entangling them in bondage. Placing the yoke upon those who should be set free.
panel: The order God gave | The Israelites in Egypt were not told to change their ways first. To become holy first. God is not the author of confusion.

# from 12911, 8550
--- Rest in Christ
big: Hebrews 4:10
p: The Sabbath has always been a picture of Christ, and the rest we have in Jesus. And the prohibition against working on that day was to illustrate that we contribute nothing to our salvation except to honor His sacrifice by trusting on Him to justify us before God.
p: Using our own works to enter into His rest is a sign of unbelief that He did it all. We rest in His work, not our own.

=== In the Gospels and Acts
# from 9249
--- Thy faith hath saved thee
big: Luke 7:50
p: Jesus flat out says her love for Him is due to her having been forgiven already. She isn’t saved because she showed Him love and hospitality, with humility and sorrow for the sins she’s done. **Her faith saved her. The love she showed Him followed.**
panel-warn: Simon the Pharisee | Simon the Pharisee, who believed he was righteous by his works, his keeping the vain traditions and ceremony of men, along with the letter of the law, couldn’t come to be saved, lacking the faith. [[Luke 7:39-47]]

# from 3071
--- What must I do to be saved?
scripture: Acts 16:30-31 | mark: Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be saved
panel-warn: What Paul did not say | He doesn’t tell him he must repent of his sins, or surrender his life to the Lord Jesus and have his fruit inspected by others. He doesn’t tell him he must join a certain Church, or attend mass, or receive sacraments.
panel: What Paul did say | Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be saved. Simple as. We are saved by faith alone, plus nothing minus nothing.

# from 3028, 6454
--- One gospel, no added rite
big: Acts 15:11
p: This is the Gospel of faith. Peter’s doctrine does not differ from Paul’s and neither is different from what Jesus preached.
lit: Is baptism required? | Mark 16:16 | This verse is often used to create the false doctrine of baptism being required for salvation, ignoring that the either/or condition is belief.
rev: The condition is belief | Mark 16:16; John 3:18 | Baptism is the outward sign that we may assume someone has professed Christ. Those who believe are saved, those who don’t are damned.

=== Adding works
# from 4511, 4421
--- Christ shall profit you nothing
scripture: Galatians 5:1-4 | mark: Christ shall profit you nothing
p: If they trust in their circumcision to justify them, even partially, then Christ will profit them nothing. This could be any other work of the flesh you’re trusting to save you, even if it is added to faith.
panel-warn: Added works | Adding baptism, turning from sin, church membership and attendance, rites of man, communion... Christ profits them nothing.
panel: Not justified by the law | Salvation comes only in faith that God’s grace has given us His only begotten Son, through whom is remission of sins. Period. [[Galatians 2:16]]

# from 9476, 11290, 5032
--- In our own filthy rags
lit: Lord, Lord | Matthew 7:21-23 | Many unsaved people trapped in false doctrine twist this verse to mean you must do works to be saved.
rev: The will of the Father | John 6:40 | But what is the will of the Father? Jesus tells us.
p: Being in proximity to Christ isn’t the same as believing on Christ. Doing works in His name, eating supper, His work done in your streets, in your church or even calling Him Lord, isn’t sufficient to be saved.
p: You can’t be saved by being the son or daughter of a saved Christian. You can’t be saved by going to a Christian church, partaking in the Lord’s supper, or by trying to show up at the wedding feast in your own attire, clothed in the filthy rags of your own righteousness. [[Matthew 22:11-13]] [[Isaiah 64:6]]

# from 10872, 11140
--- A zeal not according to knowledge
scripture: Romans 10:2-4 | mark: Christ is the end of the law for righteousness to every one that believeth
p: This same prayer and sad refrain could apply to so many zealous Catholics and Orthodox, Lordshippers and Repent-of-your-sins types. They have a zeal for God, but go about to set up their own righteousness to their destruction.
callout: All those who seek to establish their own righteousness, who deny the eternal gift, who make grace into some sort of rewards system in a game, rather than the gift of God given in the blood of His only begotten Son, seek to rob God of His glory.

# from 12058, 14781, 12169
--- “Easy believism”
panel-warn: The accusation | People who use the term “easy believism” to derisively mock the simple Gospel of grace and reconciliation, are trying to keep men under the yoke of bondage. They deny that Jesus paid it all. They add burdens grievous to be borne, and lay them on men’s shoulders.
panel: The answer | If believing the Gospel for salvation were “easy,” then why do so many people struggle with trusting in Christ Jesus alone for their salvation? Believing on Christ alone for salvation is the narrow way. The strait gate. [[Matthew 7:13-14]]
callout: Salvation is easy, from a works standpoint because it doesn’t require any effort from us to believe that Jesus paid it all. But it is hard from a human standpoint, letting go of all the burdens that keep us from passing through.

=== Good works in their place
# from 6040, 13221
--- Careful to maintain good works
scripture: Titus 3:5-8 | mark: Not by works of righteousness which we have done; they which have believed in God might be careful to maintain good works
p: This is the Biblical Doctrine of good works. That they which *have believed*, past tense, in the Gospel that was just laid out, *might* do them and be profitable to others.
callout-honest: And no, they aren’t automatic, as some false prophets preach, for if they were then we wouldn’t need so much encouragement to commit ourselves to them.

# from 806, 1957
--- Saved as we are
big: Romans 5:8
p: We are dead to sin as saved believers. The spirit does work in us the more we grow closer to God, to help remove the thorns in our hearts as we become more sanctified, praise God! But we are saved just as we are, though we still are sinners.
p: Unable to understand the difference between salvation and sanctification, the faith that saves and the love that shines from the saved. [[John 14:15]]

=== Closing
# from 8964, 10780, 10750, 11429, 4511, 6040, 12272
--- Grace, not works
point: Grace is a gift | The unearned, unmerited, undeserved gift given by God from His mercy and love.
point: No flesh justified by works | It is impossible for man to work their way to Heaven.
point: The same from the beginning | Abel’s lamb, Abraham’s faith, the Passover blood: salvation is front loaded and found only by faith.
point: Adding works | Even partially, Christ will profit them nothing.
point: Good works follow | For those who have already believed, to be profitable to others.
take: Plus nothing. Minus nothing.

# from 903
--- Call upon the name of the Lord
big: Romans 10:13
p: If you believe that God so loved you that he sent His only begotten Son, Jesus Christ, to live, die and be raised again so that all who believe on Him have eternal life, that can never be taken away or lost, never earned or deserved, given in grace, then confess with thy mouth, call upon the name of the Lord and be saved.

